## 31.1 Semaphores: A Definition

A semaphore is an object with an integer value that we can manipulate with two routines; in the POSIX standard, these routines are sem\_- wait() and sem\_post()<sup>1</sup>. Because the initial value of the semaphore determines its behavior, before calling any other routine to interact with the semaphore, we must first initialize it to some value, as the code in Figure 31.1 does.

```c
#include <semaphore.h>
sem_t s;
sem_init(&s, 0, 1);
```

